      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Using labelled microspheres, the effect of norepinephrine (NE) infusions (15 microgram and 30 microgram/min) on coronary blood flow and its intramyocardial distribution during ischemia was studied. The results reported here show that in the ischemic myocardium, the ratio of endocardial to epicardial flow was 0.67. This value became 1.0 in dogs receiving NE at a dose of 30 microgram/min. Since an adrenergic discharge is known to accompany angina in man, these data suggest that an imbalance between the endocardial and epicardial blood flow might not be present in this clinical condition."},
